  "correctness_argument": "Every bacterial gene-perturbation leaf before this change requires systematic_gene_name to be a locus tag of a pinned assembly (_validate_bacterial_locus_tag), so a loader must resolve a released strain name through a genome annotation before it can store a record, and the genome then decides which records exist: a name the annotation lacks, a released allele with no genomic coordinates, or two released rows under one label cannot be stored. The owner rule of 2026-10-12 is that ingestion consumes the raw data and the genome never gates a record (owner, 11:40 CDT, relayed: 'even for bacteria the data is the data! data ingestion is about consuming raw data.'). Nichols 2011 Table S2 (si/mmc2.xls, sha256 54be9cbc...) labels its 3,979 strains by ECK accession and upper-case symbol and states what each array is by a label suffix; the Extended Experimental Procedures give the composition ('leaving a total of 3979 strains in the final dataset (3737 Keio, 117 SPA, 5 DAS, 9 alleles, 9 linked controls, 2 truncations, and 100 sRNAs).'). Measured on the release: 41 ECK-only labels and the ECK5000-series sRNA labels are in no BW25113 annotation, 9 designed alleles are released as a protein change only (LPXC(G210S)), and 12 labels head two rows. BacterialReleasedStrainPerturbation stores one gene of such a strain exactly as released: the source's identifier, its gene name, its whole strain label and the class the label states (ReleasedStrainKind, each with an SO pair the schema already pins), with no derived locus tag and no resolution status. It is strictly additive: no existing leaf, field or validator changes, the placed leaves keep their locus-tag contract, and the new leaf refuses a locus tag of any namespace so one kind of record never sits in two classes. It is more correct than the alternatives because the record states exactly what the source states and nothing a lookup supplied, and a crosswalk to an annotation stays a separate, later act. Measured: EnvChemgenNichols2011Dataset stores 1,286,962 records, one per non-empty Table S2 cell (3,979 x 324 = 1,289,196 cells, 2,234 empty). The union widening re-stales every store whose closure holds GenePerturbationType (110 loader groups, 0 breaking, scripts/schema_impact_check.py --base origin/main); the stores are rebuilt in the KG 4.0 full rebuild.",
  "measurement_type_decision": false,
